# Review package: batch 4, slice limits

## ceb0e8a3 Count failed sign-ins in the database, per address too, so a restart does not reset them

The limits on sign-ins and invites live in the database: 30 failed sign-ins per address an hour across all emails, with
today's limits per email kept. The count takes an advisory lock, so a hundred tries at once cannot slip past it. The logic
of the limits is a pure function with direct tests. A restart no longer forgives a guesser.

